      "message": "This is reintroduced again in patchset 10: `rdma_nldev_index_from_name()` performs a separate device dump before the port dump. I agree that the kernel requires `RDMA_NLDEV_ATTR_DEV_INDEX` for `RDMA_NLDEV_CMD_PORT_GET`, but we already have the matching `ibv_device` here. Could we use `ibv_get_device_index(dev_list[i])`, pass that index to `rdma_nldev_port_from_ifname()`, and remove the device dump/name-to-index parser? That preserves the required filter while leaving only one netlink dump.",
